# Copy

Visitors are runners, not engineers. UI text is product, not debug output. Playful tone allowed (see `theme.mdc`) — never at the cost of clarity.

## Never leak the implementation

- no raw enum / slug / status / identifier values — map through a label constant (`READY_FOR_PICKUP` → `Ready to collect at Monday’s run`)
- no shell commands, file paths, env var names, or CMS field names
- no stack traces or provider error strings verbatim — summarise
- pair a raw id with its human name when the id must show (`Order 1000000`)
- full-page errors: **error-pages** rule (sentence-case H1, no HTTP codes, no red)

## States name the fix

- errors say what to do next, not only what broke
- empty states say what will fill them and offer the action (empty basket → link to merchandise)
- disabled controls say why, next to the control
- every list has designed empty, loading, and error copy

## Voice

- second person, active voice, present tense
- Title Case for headings, buttons, labels; sentence case for body and helper text
- numerals for counts (`3 items`)
- specific button labels naming the action (`Pay With Stripe`, not `Continue` / `Submit` / `OK`)
- no `Are you sure?` — state the consequence

## Characters

- `…` not `...`
- curly quotes `’` `“` `”`
- non-breaking space between value and unit or key (`18:30 Mon`)
- loading text and placeholders end with `…`
- placeholders show an example, not a restatement of the label
- `Intl.DateTimeFormat` / `Intl.NumberFormat` — never hand-rolled formats
